      "author": "Péter Soós",
      "maintainer": "Péter Soós",
      "sentence": "One DS18B20-compatible 1-Wire temperature sensor: address-based reads, classified errors, clone identification.",
      "paragraph": "Reads by ROM address after a broadcast conversion, never by bus index. Keeps DallasTemperature's raw error codes apart, so a power-on reset (the \"85 °C\" value), weak parasite power, a disconnected sensor and an out-of-range value each have their own error. Identifies genuine Maxim parts and clones via CheckDS18B20 and restores the scratchpad afterwards. Address formatting and CRC-checked parsing, a one-call status copy, no dynamic allocation, host-testable.",
      "category": "Sensors",
      "architectures": [
        "esp32",
        "esp8266",
        "avr"
      ],
      "license": "MIT",
      "depends": [
        "OneWire",
        "DallasTemperature",
        "CheckDS18B20"
      ],
      "download_url": "https://downloads.arduino.cc/libraries/github.com/soosp/DS18B20Sensor-0.1.0.zip",
      "size": 27981,
